config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_PZEM_016
	bool "Domoticz plugin: PZEM-016 (Modbus RS-485)"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_PYSERIAL
	default n
	help
		readings of the PZEM-016 energy monitors (voltage, current, power, energy) (it ships its own copy of minimalmodbus and uses pyserial for the RS-485 port).

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/domoticz-pzem-016, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		Setup -> Hardware -> PZEM-016, enter the serial port and the Modbus address.

		Licensed upstream (LICENSE is installed with the plugin). The
		repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a pinned commit of
		the default branch.
